From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: At30c <PabloAtsoc9993@outlook.com>
Date: Tue, 06 Oct 2026 11:05:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] bpf: verifier: accept PTR_TO_MEM for helper memory pointers

The ring buffer implementation is already present in this tree, including
bpf_ringbuf_reserve() returning RET_PTR_TO_ALLOC_MEM_OR_NULL and the
PTR_TO_MEM/PTR_TO_MEM_OR_NULL register tracking in check_mem_access(),
where every access is bounds checked against reg->mem_size.

However check_func_arg() still restricts ARG_PTR_TO_MEM,
ARG_PTR_TO_MEM_OR_NULL and ARG_PTR_TO_UNINIT_MEM to packet pointers,
PTR_TO_MAP_VALUE and PTR_TO_STACK. A pointer handed out by
bpf_ringbuf_reserve() is therefore rejected before the helper ever runs,
which makes the common "reserve, then fill the record with
bpf_probe_read()/bpf_probe_read_str()" pattern impossible to verify:

  R1 type=mem expected=fp

This is what Android 17 bpfloader hits while loading bpfMemEvents.bpf:

  prog 'tracepoint_oom_mark_victim_ams': failed to load: -13
  39: (85) call bpf_probe_read_str#45
      R1 type=mem expected=fp

Mirror upstream and allow PTR_TO_MEM for the memory pointer argument
types. No new register type is introduced: the register can only be
produced by bpf_ringbuf_reserve(), it is bounded by the same mem_size
accounting that already governs direct loads and stores, and
meta->raw_mode keeps ARG_PTR_TO_UNINIT_MEM semantics intact.

---
 kernel/bpf/verifier.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/kernel/bpf/verifier.c b/kernel/bpf/verifier.c
index 6bb39abd809e..e0df881ae841 100644
--- a/kernel/bpf/verifier.c
+++ b/kernel/bpf/verifier.c
@@ -2046,6 +2046,7 @@ static int check_func_arg(struct bpf_verifier_env *env, u32 regno,
 			/* final test in check_stack_boundary() */;
 		else if (!type_is_pkt_pointer(type) &&
 			 type != PTR_TO_MAP_VALUE &&
+			 type != PTR_TO_MEM &&
 			 type != expected_type)
 			goto err_type;
 		meta->raw_mode = arg_type == ARG_PTR_TO_UNINIT_MEM;
